The main design choice is clear now: the queue should stay table-backed and decision routing should continue through `ConsolidationProposal::apply/reject`. The only open integration question is scope representation, because organization scope exists in the newer memory graph but not in the legacy memory model that consolidation still serializes. I’m checking the smallest correct extension path before editing.
