+test result: ok. 9 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 452 filtered out; finished in 0.63s
+```
+
+Issues encountered
+- Legacy consolidation state serializes `memory::MemoryScope` as capitalized strings like `Repo`, while the new manual-review gate needs `repo` and `organization` semantics. The review queue now normalizes scope strings before classification so repo-scoped proposals gate correctly and organization-scoped proposals can be queued without extending the legacy memory enum.
+- The consolidation schema migration already handled `provenance_json` and `reverted`; this task extended that path to add `decision_reason` safely for existing databases.
+
+Final status: complete

codex
Implemented the Phase 6 manual review queue for high-scope consolidation proposals and wrote the result artifact at [T44.md](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/results/T44.md).

The change adds `ReviewQueue` and its tests in [review_queue.rs](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/review_queue.rs) and [review_queue_tests.rs](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/review_queue_tests.rs), wires low-scope auto-apply versus repo/organization gating through the consolidation runtime, extends proposal/schema metadata with `decision_reason`, and records `decided_by` / `decision_reason` on `MemoryConsolidated` events. I also added a minimal `OperatorId` type in the identity layer.

Verification ran clean:
- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/review_queue.rs`
- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/review_queue_tests.rs`
- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib consolidation::review_queue_tests`

That test run passed `9/9`.
